message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of how you can create a “card” that rotates when you hover over it using only HTML and CSS (no JavaScript).  
Feel free to copy‑paste this into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Center the container */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* Card wrapper – gives perspective so the rotation looks 3D */
.card-wrapper {
    width:300px;
    height:200px;
    perspective:800px;          /* Creates depth perception */
}

/* The actual card element */
.card {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
    transition:transform .6s ease;  /* Smooth animation */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* Hide backside when rotated away */
    border-radius:10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    color:white;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-size:1.5rem;
    text-align:center;
    padding:20px;
}

/* Styling for front */
.card .front {
    background:#3498db;            /* Blue background */
}

/* Styling for back */
.card .back {
    background:#e74c3c;            /* Red background */
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* Initially flipped */
}

/* Hover effect – flip the card */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front content -->
        <div class="front">
            <p>Front Side</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back content -->
        <div class="back">
            <p>Back Side</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a `perspective` so the 3D rotation has depth. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides, uses `transform-style: preserve-3d` to keep child elements in 3D space. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Both positioned absolutely on top of each other. `backface-visibility:hidden` hides the side facing away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Rotated 180° initially so it's hidden until the parent flips. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the whole card 180°, revealing the back side. |

You can replace the `<p>` tags with images, icons, or any other content you like. Adjust colors, sizes, or transition duration as desired. Enjoy!
